/*****************************************************************************
    tabForm -- the tabs form. Definitions only, shaped like IncantForms/Windows/firstLight
    (Tony, 2026-11-18, SEQ 700): fire it with Start(); show(tabForm); The form names no
    colour and no font: only placeholders, resolved through the look (IncantForms/Controls/styles).
    Notes below bail().
*****************************************************************************/
register(dESCRIPTIONs);
define
    tabForm=(In this example, there are two key components to a tabForm interface, the tabBAR (a block with a tabs attribute containing tab blocks). The second component is a block of body panels or cards, with each card associated with a tab. When a tab is selected its associated card is shown.#);
    tabBAR=(When you select a tab on the tabBAR, the body shown in the bodies block becomes the card named in the tab selected: so if tabOne is selected, the firstCard becomes the body, the other two card bodies are hidden. Note the use of selectFill to set the background color of the tab when a tab is selected. Here the selected tab color is matched to the color of the associated body panel but it does not have to be.#);
    ;
register(FORMs);
define
    tabSelected = 0;
    tabClick code={ selectTab(argument); };
    firstCard;
    secondCard;
    thirdCard;
    ;
define
    tabForm window closable resize x=400 y=400 width=360 height=400 fill:=pageFill title="Using Tabs"
        body
            intro height=50 fill:=pageFill border
                heading="Tabs Example" font:=headingFont align=center valign=center;
            tabBAR height=25 across font:=tabFont tabs:=tabSelected
                tabOne="One" card:=firstCard border fill:=tabFill selectFill:=cardOneFill onClick:=tabClick;
                tabTwo="Two" card:=secondCard fill:=tabFill selectFill:=cardTwoFill border onClick:=tabClick;
                tabThree="Three" card:=thirdCard fill:=tabFill selectFill:=cardThreeFill border onClick:=tabClick;
            bodies cards
                firstCard="The first tab body" border fill:=cardOneFill;
                secondCard="The second tab body" border fill:=cardTwoFill;
                thirdCard="The third tab body" border fill:=cardThreeFill;
            help describe=tabForm border height=100 fill:=tabFill;
    ;
bail();

THE CARDS ARE DECLARED FIRST (SEQ 700, measured). A tab names its card with card:=firstCard (Tony, ruling 4 of the tabs
recon), and a := in a define names a field that must already be defined: without the three declarations above the form,
each tab refused ("a := in a define names a field, and no field by this name is on the search list") and was REMOVED.
Declared first, the forms card of the same name reopens the declared one: FORMs["firstCard"] reads "The first tab body".

PLACEHOLDERS (ruling 2): tabFill, tabFont, cardOneFill, cardTwoFill, cardThreeFill, added to IncantForms/Controls/styles
with their defaultLook values (lightGreen, headerFont, green, blue, red). A tabs selectFill names its cards fill, so one
role colours both. The page and intro use pageFill (white in defaultLook; the old wall was never visible, the body covers it).

READ SINCE STROKES 2-3: tabs:=, card:=, cards and selectFill (cardsPick, in setFrame, on the laid-out copy). The selected tab
lives in tabSelected, outside the form (ruling 3). The windows closable, resize and title are inert old-GUI chrome, as in descriptions.

THE CLICK (stroke 4, SEQ 737): each tab's onClick:=tabClick fires on a click; tabClick calls utilities' selectTab, which writes
tabSelected to hold the clicked tab. clickShow(request) clicks and draws in one call:
    define
        tabThreeClick form:=tabForm field="tabThree";
        ;
    clickShow(tabThreeClick);
WHY tabClick AND NOT onClick:=selectTab: a := in a define names a field already on the search list, and show reads this file
under cOLOr fONTs sTYLEs only, so selectTab (Utilities) was refused and the three tabs REMOVED (measured). tabClick is this
form's own action, as firstLight's okClick is; its body finds selectTab when it first runs, from the clicking caller's list.
